- **P2** - app/src/test/kotlin/net/montycasa/roux/ui/lint/HiddenActionViolation.kt:270. `matchingParen` treats `)` inside a backticked identifier as syntax. For example, `val \`score)\` = "Scores"` used in `TopAppBar(title = { Text(\`score)\`) }, actions = {})` makes the matcher stop inside the identifier, so it never scans the `actions` slot.

Yes, `a<b` is also a valid comparison, so adjacency alone can leave the angle counter stuck; I couldn’t make that Boolean expression type-check as a positional argument to the current Material3 top bars, so I don’t count it as a second actionable bypass.

